#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""MK Photo Booth: your webcam with live looks, then decorate and save.

  camera-controls            open the booth (app grid: Photo Booth, Super+C)

Camera page: a live, mirrored preview; looks (Polaroid, Thermal, Pop Art,
Noir, Comic, Neon...) applied as you watch, sorted into Vintage, Artistic and
Fun with a search box; Adjust opens the webcam's own
hardware controls (brightness, contrast, saturation, gamma, sharpness, white
balance) with Reset to hardware defaults. Space or the shutter button takes
the photo, after an optional 3-2-1 countdown.

G shows nine looks at once, live (3 x 3); click one to use it.

Decorate page (the camera and its light are off here; Retake turns them
back on): type text or pick an emoji sticker, then click the photo to
place it. A placed layer can be selected and moved, resized from its
corners and turned from the knob on top (the angle shows as you turn);
bring it forward or send it back, or delete it. With a Polaroid frame,
write a caption on it; add a date stamp (90s digital, typewriter or
handwritten). Save: the photo goes to ~/Pictures/MK Booth/.

The looks come from lib/mkworkstation/photo.py; text and stickers are drawn
with Pango and cairo (colour emoji). Hardware controls use v4l2-ctl.
"""
